{
  "schema": "builder.flow/v1",
  "name": "Formative feedback tutor",
  "version": 1,
  "input_field": "submission",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "submission",
      "kind": "input",
      "label": "Submission",
      "position": {
        "x": 340,
        "y": 0
      },
      "config": {
        "field": "submission",
        "label": "The question and the student's answer",
        "max_chars": 2000,
        "required": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "teacher_check",
      "kind": "gate",
      "label": "Teacher check",
      "position": {
        "x": 340,
        "y": 160
      },
      "config": {
        "message": "An assessor and a tutor are about to read this submission. Approve it, or send it back.",
        "editable_fields": [],
        "max_turns": 1,
        "expiry_seconds": 1800
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "assess",
      "kind": "agent",
      "label": "Assess",
      "position": {
        "x": 340,
        "y": 320
      },
      "config": {
        "tier": "cheap",
        "max_iter": 2,
        "guardrail_max_retries": 2,
        "prompt_inputs": {
          "submission": "${state.submission}"
        },
        "role": "Assessor",
        "goal": "Decide whether a student's answer is correct and name the misconception behind it if it is not.",
        "backstory": "You mark secondary-school maths and science. You judge the final answer and the reasoning the student gave, and you name the specific misconception rather than saying 'careless error'.",
        "task": {
          "description": "Assess the student's answer.\n\nSUBMISSION:\n{submission}",
          "expected_output": "An object with `verdict` (exactly one of correct, partial, incorrect), `misconception` (one sentence, or 'none'), and `next_step` (what the student should try next, in one sentence).",
          "output_schema": {
            "verdict": "string",
            "misconception": "string",
            "next_step": "string"
          },
          "markdown": false,
          "async_execution": false
        },
        "llm": {
          "model": "google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite:nitro",
          "temperature": null,
          "top_p": null,
          "max_tokens": null,
          "timeout": null,
          "response_format": null,
          "frequency_penalty": null,
          "presence_penalty": null,
          "stop": [],
          "seed": null,
          "reasoning_effort": null
        },
        "max_rpm": null,
        "max_execution_time": null,
        "allow_delegation": false,
        "memory": false,
        "cache": true,
        "respect_context_window": true,
        "retry": {
          "max_retries": 0,
          "backoff_seconds": 0,
          "fallback_model": null
        },
        "system_template": null,
        "prompt_template": null,
        "response_template": null,
        "tool_failure_policy": null,
        "planning": false,
        "planning_config": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verdict",
      "kind": "transform",
      "label": "Verdict",
      "position": {
        "x": 340,
        "y": 480
      },
      "config": {
        "op": "pick",
        "args": {
          "source": "${state.out__assess}",
          "key": "verdict"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "tutor",
      "kind": "agent",
      "label": "Tutor",
      "position": {
        "x": 340,
        "y": 640
      },
      "config": {
        "tier": "cheap",
        "max_iter": 2,
        "guardrail_max_retries": 2,
        "prompt_inputs": {
          "submission": "${state.submission}",
          "assessment": "${state.out__assess}"
        },
        "role": "Tutor",
        "goal": "Write feedback that moves this student's understanding forward.",
        "backstory": "You give formative feedback, not solutions. Research on feedback is clear that telling a student the answer ends their thinking, so you name the misconception, give one hint and ask one question that lets them find the answer themselves.",
        "task": {
          "description": "A student answered the question below. An assessor has already diagnosed their answer.\n\nSUBMISSION:\n{submission}\n\nASSESSMENT:\n{assessment}\n\nWrite feedback addressed to the student.\nIf the answer is wrong or partly wrong: (1) name the misconception in one sentence, without blaming; (2) give ONE hint about the method; (3) end with ONE guiding question they can answer themselves. NEVER state the correct final answer, the correct value, or the correct term, and do not work the problem through for them.\nIf the answer is right: say specifically what they did well and ask one extension question.\nFor a 'why' or 'what' question, do not name the scientific term or quantity that answers it, even inside the hint or the question; point the student at something they can observe or check instead.\nAt most 90 words.",
          "expected_output": "At most 90 words of feedback addressed to the student, in Markdown, that does not contain the correct final answer.",
          "output_schema": null,
          "markdown": true,
          "async_execution": false
        },
        "llm": {
          "model": "google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite:nitro",
          "temperature": null,
          "top_p": null,
          "max_tokens": null,
          "timeout": null,
          "response_format": null,
          "frequency_penalty": null,
          "presence_penalty": null,
          "stop": [],
          "seed": null,
          "reasoning_effort": null
        },
        "max_rpm": null,
        "max_execution_time": null,
        "allow_delegation": false,
        "memory": false,
        "cache": true,
        "respect_context_window": true,
        "retry": {
          "max_retries": 0,
          "backoff_seconds": 0,
          "fallback_model": null
        },
        "system_template": null,
        "prompt_template": null,
        "response_template": null,
        "tool_failure_policy": null,
        "planning": false,
        "planning_config": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "report",
      "kind": "transform",
      "label": "Teacher report",
      "position": {
        "x": 340,
        "y": 800
      },
      "config": {
        "op": "format",
        "args": {
          "template": "DIAGNOSIS: {verdict}\n\nFEEDBACK FOR THE STUDENT:\n{feedback}",
          "verdict": "${state.out__verdict}",
          "feedback": "${state.out__tutor}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "final",
      "kind": "output",
      "label": "Feedback",
      "position": {
        "x": 340,
        "y": 960
      },
      "config": {
        "body_key": "markdown_body",
        "source": "${state.out__report}"
      }
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
      "id": "e1",
      "source": "submission",
      "source_port": "out",
      "target": "teacher_check",
      "target_port": "in"
    },
    {
      "id": "e2",
      "source": "teacher_check",
      "source_port": "approve",
      "target": "assess",
      "target_port": "in"
    },
    {
      "id": "e3",
      "source": "assess",
      "source_port": "out",
      "target": "verdict",
      "target_port": "in"
    },
    {
      "id": "e4",
      "source": "verdict",
      "source_port": "out",
      "target": "tutor",
      "target_port": "in"
    },
    {
      "id": "e5",
      "source": "tutor",
      "source_port": "out",
      "target": "report",
      "target_port": "in"
    },
    {
      "id": "e6",
      "source": "report",
      "source_port": "out",
      "target": "final",
      "target_port": "in"
    }
  ],
  "joins": {},
  "budget": null
}
